# TPSS on helium with regularized (nuclear-cusp-free) orbitals.
#
# The meta-GGA counterpart of nemo_he_pbe, and the deck that covers meta-GGA on
# the nemo path. Three things had to exist for this to run at all, none of which
# the moldft path needs:
#
#   * tau from the nemos. tau is an orbital functional, and with psi = R F the
#     product rule gives grad psi = R (grad F - U1 F), so
#         tau = 1/2 R^2 sum_i w_i |grad F_i - U1 F_i|^2
#     with U1 = -grad(R)/R analytic and precomputed. Only the cusp-free F is
#     differentiated numerically -- forming psi = R F and differentiating that
#     would put the nuclear cusp straight back under the derivative operator.
#
#   * the non-multiplicative term, divided by R. nemo's equations are for F, so
#     what is needed is R^{-1}[-1/2 div(v_tau grad(R F))]. With
#     W = v_tau (grad F - U1 F) and div(R W) = R (div W - U1.W) the R factors
#     cancel exactly, giving -1/2 (div W - U1.W) -- no division by R anywhere.
#
#   * a place to put it. nemo registers the xc contribution as a
#     LocalPotentialOperator, which cannot carry a differential operator; the
#     term is added to the nemo-side potentials in compute_nemo_potentials
#     instead. Nemo::make_fock_operator therefore refuses a meta-GGA outright
#     rather than returning a Fock operator that silently drops it.
#
# CROSS-CHECK, which is what makes this deck a real test rather than a smoke
# test. The same system and functional through `--wf=scf` (moldft) builds tau by
# differentiating the physical orbitals across the cusp, with no U1 anywhere --
# a completely different code path to the same physics. Tightened to
# `protocol [1e-4, 1e-6, 1e-8]` the two agree to ~1e-08 at -2.9096637. A sign
# error or a missing term in either the tau product rule or the R cancellation
# would show up there immediately, and nothing else in the tree would catch it.
#
# EXTERNAL ANCHOR. TURBOMOLE TPSS/aug-cc-pV6Z, grid m5, is -2.90964927, so the
# converged MRA value sits 14.4 uHa below the largest Gaussian basis -- the same
# sign and magnitude as the closed-shell PBE case (7.9 uHa), with the larger
# offset expected of a meta-GGA, and reproducing an independent earlier He/TPSS
# cross-check to the digit.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc --wf=nemo nemo_he_tpss.in)

dft
    xc       tpss
    k        7
    maxiter  20
    econv    1e-5
    dconv    1e-3
end

nemo
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    He  0.0  0.0  0.0
end
